# Confirm intent before you edit

Chris is fast to review and precise when the words are locked. Guessing the wrong control wastes the session.

1. Name the thing you think he means, in his words. Point at the screenshot or label if you have one.
2. If two things could match (week strip vs Job/Mo–Sa bar, All Stages vs Back to job), ask which.
3. State the change in one short list. No extra polish.
4. Wait for **OK**. Do not edit, commit, or push before that.
5. Then do only that. Preview. Stop.

Do not invent layout, spacing, type, or extra chrome. If it is not specified, ask. Do not "improve" design on the way through.

Wrong this session: treating "date bar" as the Job/Mo–Sa header, adding a second black bar, coding before OK.

Right: "Your date bar = Prev / Sep 7–12 / Next. Job/Mo–Sa stays. Say OK."
